  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.963pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(107.098pt, 510.008pt, " Extreme Ultraviolet Lithography")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Medi", size: 11.955pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 539.689pt, "1")
  #line-at(89.933pt, 539.689pt, "Introduction")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.933pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 563.574pt, "Extreme ultraviolet lithography is a critical component in the development of semiconductor manufacturing processes.")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.862pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(71.691pt, 574.483pt, "This technology enables the creation of smaller and more advanced semiconductor chips by utilizing shorter wavelengths")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.978pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 585.392pt, "of light to etch intricate designs onto silicon wafers.")
  #line-at(282.302pt, 585.392pt, "Through this method, manufacturers are able to continue scaling")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.963pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 596.302pt, "down the size of transistors in accordance with Moore’s Law.")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.862pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 612.69pt, "Integrated circuits are made using EUV lithography, a process analogous to photographic printing, in which the patterns")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 10.052pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 623.599pt, "that will become layers of an integrated circuit are exposed on a semiconductor wafer, one layer at a time.")
  #line-at(503.144pt, 623.599pt, "The light")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 10.062pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 634.508pt, "pattern")
  #line-at(103.512pt, 634.508pt, "on")
  #line-at(116.976pt, 634.508pt, "the")
  #line-at(132.687pt, 634.508pt, "wafer")
  #line-at(159.016pt, 634.508pt, "is")
  #line-at(169.086pt, 634.508pt, "formed")
  #line-at(201.726pt, 634.508pt, "due")
  #line-at(219.702pt, 634.508pt, "to")
  #line-at(230.901pt, 634.508pt, "the")
  #line-at(246.621pt, 634.508pt, "reflection")
  #line-at(288.295pt, 634.508pt, "of")
  #line-at(300.052pt, 634.508pt, "EUV")
  #line-at(324.237pt, 634.508pt, "electromagnetic")
  #line-at(392.434pt, 634.508pt, "beam")
  #line-at(417.737pt, 634.508pt, "from")
  #line-at(440.794pt, 634.508pt, "the")
  #line-at(456.504pt, 634.508pt, "mask")
  #line-at(481.248pt, 634.508pt, "(see")
  #line-at(500.912pt, 634.508pt, "Figure")
  #line-at(530.737pt, 634.508pt, "1).")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.878pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 645.417pt, "Modern integrated circuits require more than 80 different masks in their production.")
  #line-at(404.147pt, 645.417pt, "Due to diffraction and interference")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 10.062pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 656.326pt, "phenomena,")
  #line-at(124.455pt, 656.326pt, "the patterns on the mask do not match the light pattern on the wafer (see Figure 1 (a)).")
  #line-at(485.781pt, 656.326pt, "To obtain the")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.933pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 667.236pt, "desired pattern on the wafer, a multi-stage technology of optical proximity correction (OPC) of mask is used (Figure 1")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.923pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(71.671pt, 678.145pt, "(b)).")
  #line-at(92.079pt, 678.145pt, "One of the stages of optical approximation correction is calculating electromagnetic fields in the area of the mask")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.903pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 689.054pt, "location.")
  #line-at(109.285pt, 689.054pt, "The diffracted electromagnetic waves can be calculated rigorously by using electromagnetic (EM) simulators.")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 9.963pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 699.963pt, "However, these calculations require massive computational resources.")
  #set text(font: "CMSY6", size: 5.978pt, weight: "regular", style: "italic", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(83.822pt, 716.191pt, "∗")
  #set text(font: "NimbusRomNo9L-Regu", size: 8.966pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
